  m_Name: Disease_SugarcaneRedRot
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  diseaseId: red_rot
  diseaseName: Red Rot
  aiLabelAliases:
  - sugarcane_red_rot
  - RedRot
  - Red Rot
  - sugarcane red rot
  - Sugarcane___Red_rot
  pathogenType: 0
  pathogen: Colletotrichum falcatum
  affectedPart: 0
  sources:
  - 'Sugarcane Leaf Disease Dataset (Mendeley Data) class: RedRot, Red Rot, sugarcane
    red rot'
  - 'Content: general plant-pathology knowledge (APS disease compendia, university
    extension guides, UC IPM); not reviewed by a plant pathologist.'
  description: 'The most destructive fungal disease of sugarcane: it rots the inside
    of the cane red and marks the leaf midribs.'
  causes: Spores spread in infected setts, by rain and irrigation water, and through
    borer holes; waterlogging and susceptible varieties favour it.
  effectOnPlant: Infected canes dry out and lose their sugar.
  untreatedOutcome: Whole fields can be lost with susceptible varieties.
  symptoms:
  - Long, blood-red lesions along the leaf midrib, later with straw-coloured centres
  - Upper leaves yellow and dry from the tips
  - Split canes are red inside with white patches and smell sour
  supportingFeatureIds:
  - leaf_spots
  - leaf_color
  - yellowing
  moderateSeverityThreshold: 0.35
  severeSeverityThreshold: 0.7
  treatmentPlan: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 206181aaae4a11147b6052437491a5be, type: 2}
  preventionPlan: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 606dd0bcc056895458956e6e4a5185f1, type: 2}
  simulationProfile: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f2dfb106809e2e48b0d5678b61aaa3a, type: 2}
  lifecycleStages:
  - The fungus comes in on infected setts.
  - Spores spread by water and wind.
  - Red lesions form on the midribs; canes rot inside.
  - Canes dry; spores spread to new plantings.
  conditionFactors:
  - Infected seed cane.
  - Waterlogging.
  - Borer damage.
  - Susceptible varieties.
  referencePhotos: []
  lesionLabel: Red midrib lesion
  haloLabel: Straw centre
  areaLabel: Drying leaf
